e implicated blob left both broad and narrow history reads healthy. That later batched-empty / narrow-success recurrence was a separate fixture-contract defect fixed by merged Gerrit 1828. This ticket preserves the unresolved ENOENT work so the repaired recurrence ticket does not falsely claim to solve it.\n\n## Plan\n- On the next organic recurrence, collect the Gerrit 1769 forensic block (fsck, count-objects, object listing with mtimes, and GIT_* environment).\n- Identify and deterministically reproduce the process or environment mechanism that removes or hides a freshly committed reachable loose object.\n- Add a RED regression for the proven mechanism, fix the mechanism class without weakening the fixture topology, and prove GREEN plus exact-defect mutation coverage.\n- Run the repository gates and land through Gerrit before closing.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] An organic recurrence supplies the captured object-store forensic block, or an equivalent deterministic local reproduction identifies the deleter.\n- [ ] The deleting or object-hiding mechanism is proven rather than inferred from the invalid-object signature alone.\n- [ ] A behavioral regression is observed RED before the class fix and GREEN afterward.\n- [ ] The exact-defect mutation returns the regression to RED.\n- [ ] Repository lint, typecheck, full tests, Gerrit LLM-Review, and Verified gates pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"a375218d-ee93-446c-92c7-cad58d75fa38","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"blocked","tags":["test","flaky"],"ticket_id":"0f8f-8178-96b4-4901","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Root-cause unresolved loose-object ENOENT in authorship fixture merge","verify_commands":[